<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:11:25Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Chase outage disrupts online banking and Zelle payments in United States</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c17cd578c5378be69ac433dfd0f8d5e92b308d1867eb06c06f5f9f2b3da12483</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:10:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T22:40:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-chase-outage-disrupts-online-banking-and-zelle-payments-in-united-states-us-software--69cbbbd1d139.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-chase-outage-disrupts-online-banking-and-zelle-payments-in-united-states-us-software" /><summary type="html">American users of several major banking apps and online portals reported outages on Monday, according to the monitoring site Downdetector.com, with one institution ruling out a cyberattack as the cause. Among those affected by the outages were Bank of America, JPMorgan Chase and the popular money transfer app Zelle.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says he needs funding for air traffic control after ground stop</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a8481a74613af8998a26ace91a20ef874ba5d957686b5913ce081dd4d4f891f</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:11:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T22:01:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-says-he-needs-funding-for-air-traffic-control-after-ground-stop--48f92ae1d591.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-says-he-needs-funding-for-air-traffic-control-after-ground-stop" /><summary type="html">US ​President ​Donald Trump, pressed on a ​technology ‌failure ⁠that ‌grounded thousands of ⁠flights last week, ​on ‌Monday told reporters ‌that ​the government needed funding for upgrade ​to ​air traffic ​control equipment. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis speaks with Sheldon Jacobson, Professor of Computer Science at the University of Illinois. He explains that "the Republicans have had full control of the House and the Senate since the President came in. They controlled everything. If they needed the money and wanted the money they could have approved the money. The fact that they didn't, in the the different bills that have been passed, suggests that it's more than just money that is going on here".</summary></entry><entry><title>US judge strikes down Trump visa restrictions on foreign students, journalists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0fe006c47f251dc60be90c2848887d4baa1f780d87f7cf22a6c1b03ef419677b</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:11:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T21:23:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-us-judge-strikes-down-trump-visa-restrictions-on-foreign-students-journalists--89359086d5e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-us-judge-strikes-down-trump-visa-restrictions-on-foreign-students-journalists" /><summary type="html">A US federal judge has struck down a Trump administration policy that would have sharply limited the length of time foreign students and journalists could stay in the country, ruling that the proposed restrictions were unlawful and would undermine opportunities for international education.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>November 17 blackout hoax: How a conspiracy theory went viral around the world</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0a3644e8c2b579a591df639c47a5a98b80aedefa0ce138284c7471999ec2835</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:11:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T20:50:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261116-november-17-blackout-hoax-how-a-conspiracy-theory-went-viral-around-the-world--0b2ddebc84cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261116-november-17-blackout-hoax-how-a-conspiracy-theory-went-viral-around-the-world" /><summary type="html">A conspiracy theory claiming a worldwide “blackout” will hit on November 17 has spread across social media, cutting electricity, internet and banking services. The rumour stems from a routine US FEMA emergency alert test, but was amplified by cryptocurrency accounts, misleading claims about EU preparedness advice and references to The Simpsons. Recent technology outages, flight disruptions and cyberattacks have added to public anxiety, helping turn a routine test into a global blackout hoax.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Pope concludes South America homecoming, reassures faithful after cancer scare</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18622000feac15032e3d84c9bae081dd11f2f684d8a80f8bfb2bb1359461c3ad</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:11:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T20:50:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-pope-concludes-south-america-homecoming-reassures-faithful-after-cancer-scare--0f38c5877379.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-pope-concludes-south-america-homecoming-reassures-faithful-after-cancer-scare" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV finished Monday his 12-day tour of Uruguay, Argentina and Peru reiterating his advocacy for social justice, environmental protection and the importance of community. Just a month after undergoing lung cancer surgery, the 71-year-old pontiff drew millions of faithful across South America, where he spent nearly two decades as a missionary.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>The new faces of the US Congress</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bee2e145d4db90a84eece66ba04b949318c1cc690eaef0dd5abb7cf215247319</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:11:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T20:36:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/the-new-faces-of-the-us-congress--c1a20de87eae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/the-new-faces-of-the-us-congress" /><summary type="html">The United States Congress is about to welcome dozens of new faces. A majority of them, Democratic, after the "blue wave" in the midterm elections. FRANCE 24's Washington correspondent Fraser Jackson catches up with one of these new lawmakers as they go through orientation as they prepare to take office in January. He speaks with Katy Padilla Stout, U.S. Representative-elect for Texas's 23rd congressional district.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mexican drug trade 'boss of bosses' Miguel Angel Felix Gallardo dies at 80</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:617014b314beb549448bdd9a6700790606e94187a3af75c7c2de886ef3f38fbb</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T22:48:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-miguel-angel-felix-gallardo-mexican-drug-lord-dies--90e53724e9b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-miguel-angel-felix-gallardo-mexican-drug-lord-dies" /><summary type="html">Miguel Angel Felix Gallardo, a founder of Mexico’s Guadalajara drug cartel known as the “boss of bosses”, died in hospital on Sunday aged 80 after suffering multiple organ failure, Jalisco state’s security ministry said. Imprisoned since 1989, he had been transferred from prison to the hospital two days before his death.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Record number of women elected' to US Congress &amp; governorships in midterm elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:692dd63ef4f6cc3ebd41ef9585ff73f2aa845c8559884e2cb9bf52e28936a3ad</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T15:40:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-record-number-of-women-elected-to-us-congress-governorships-across-country-in-midterm-elect--7efef40d71de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-record-number-of-women-elected-to-us-congress-governorships-across-country-in-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">Following the 2026 US midterm elections, Gavin Lee welcomes Politico Senior National Politics Reporter Lauren Fedor to discuss the growing number of Democratic women elected to Congress and governorships, particularly mothers of young children.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Jensen Huang: The French Connection</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d71bd430e5d2cbee5334a4bfd5e3c2c631dd68a109a78da49b2bd704490bb24</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T15:03:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-jensen-huang-the-french-connection--c681b71603cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-jensen-huang-the-french-connection" /><summary type="html">President Trump is heading to Asia in a few days' time, where he is due to meet President Putin and President Xi. But there could be one fewer tech giant at the table: Jensen Huang, who has resigned from Nvidia amid a suspected espionage affair.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>US probes nationwide flights stoppage as travel disruptions persist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02d99be26a3a0543b290dba5fc7483bee8f0504e64caaee6f54512d663aacdeb</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T14:09:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-probes-nationwide-flights-stoppage-as-travel-disruptions-persist--66080e063e19.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-probes-nationwide-flights-stoppage-as-travel-disruptions-persist" /><summary type="html">US air travel is expected to return to normal this Sunday, following a nationwide ground stop Friday night that stranded hundreds of thousands of passengers and disrupted travel worldwide. The Trump administration blamed the incident on a botched replacement of old copper wire communication lines and said there was no evidence this was a cyberattack. The ground stop now raises questions about the country's aging infrastructure and lawmakers are calling for an investigation. Analysis by Philip Mann, aviation expert at Vector Strategic Consulting.</summary></entry><entry><title>Air travel issues persist in the US after nationwide ground stop</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8567b72872b39c9c7373794b1010e55bde12ba9203bd4c3dbc2312dc9a322aee</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T12:12:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/air-travel-issues-persist-in-the-us-after-nationwide-ground-stop--ae8922ebd6d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/air-travel-issues-persist-in-the-us-after-nationwide-ground-stop" /><summary type="html">After almost five hours of grounded flights in the US, flights have resumed. However, passengers are still waiting and wading through tough logistics to get to their destinations after massive delays and cancelled flights. Details by Simon Moritz.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope laments poverty-stricken Inca communities as locals leave Peru</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c0653c39cc688ed97b5a6a23a5da38972a8f8d765f82d051679acf195daff37</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T10:55:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-pope-laments-poverty-stricken-inca-communities-as-locals-leave-peru--5c41da65bfa4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-pope-laments-poverty-stricken-inca-communities-as-locals-leave-peru" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV on Sunday will traverse the length of Peru in what marks the penultimate day of his Latin American tour. The leader of the Catholic church – who underwent cancer surgery just a month ago – warned that Peru's remote Inca communities are under threat as poverty continues to drive locals out of their homeland in search of better futures.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>SpaceX makes rocketry history by recapturing massive reusable rocketship</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:553b934b98a5278d96aa9af2507fe4d4455f9503a40ffb8148b61806d67cea99</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T09:42:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spacex-makes-rocketry-history-by-recapturing-massive-reusable-rocketship--f03cae991aee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spacex-makes-rocketry-history-by-recapturing-massive-reusable-rocketship" /><summary type="html">After failing to catch a booster yesterday, SpaceX managed to recapture its massive reusable rocketship, "Starship" for the first time. Smaller previous models have successfully relanded but they require heavy legs and aren't fully reusable. Story by Daniel Quinlan.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo urges stop to Amazon deforestation, demands justice for slain Indigenous leaders</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2ca977096eac96f95acc65d4cd5fe95bca369f8e215c7ab850cd4ddaf318b14</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T05:51:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-pope-leo-visits-peru-s-high-altitude-cusco-testing-recovery-from-lung-cancer--3fbefede09b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-pope-leo-visits-peru-s-high-altitude-cusco-testing-recovery-from-lung-cancer" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV travelled across Peru on Sunday to visit communities high in the Andes mountains and deep in the Amazon rainforest, testing his recovery from lung cancer surgery a month ago. The pontiff condemned the exploitation of the Amazon and urged Catholics to oppose "with perseverance" the deforestation and pollution caused by gold and oil production in the world's largest rainforest.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Elon Musk's SpaceX aborts booster recovery due to technical issues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71afa7a105152e141945b102f3fc7178b638fa8e6d7eec2d3964b9fc25a8fc13</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T17:33:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/elon-musk-s-spacex-aborts-booster-recovery-due-to-technical-issues--6420a1fd1469.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/elon-musk-s-spacex-aborts-booster-recovery-due-to-technical-issues" /><summary type="html">Elon Musk's SpaceX is in the midst of a 15th test-flight of its Starship rocket. The company was hoping to pull off the first-ever "double catch" - with both the booster and the ship itself coming safely back down to earth. Instead, an unspecified problem forced the company to abort recovery of the booster, which was diverted from its return path and crashed down into the Gulf of Mexico. Analysis by journalist Frédéric Castel, based in Bosa Chica, Texas, USA.</summary></entry><entry><title>Washington divided over how to deal with fallout from the Nvidia case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dab1411664948292e92c1b88cc45d3ef462e8677a54822afb5c04c0f021751c0</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T17:21:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/washington-divided-over-how-to-deal-with-fallout-from-the-nvidia-case--10e578662d3b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/washington-divided-over-how-to-deal-with-fallout-from-the-nvidia-case" /><summary type="html">After the fall, the fallout. US government agencies are squabbling after AI leader Jensen Huang stepped down from chips giant Nvidia in disgrace. The Treasury says it wanted to blacklist a Singapore company at the heart of the scandal, but the Commerce Department didn't act. Megaspeed was run by suspected Chinese spy Alice Huang, who reportedly had an affair with Jensen Huang. Details by Peter O'Brien.</summary></entry><entry><title>US: What exactly caused the longest nationwide ground stop in 25 years?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8dd6dd72c5074e54dcd72d49df49526a29deba13252196e200d3f902e36b7d76</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T16:35:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-what-exactly-caused-the-longest-nationwide-ground-stop-in-25-years--773fa7defb8c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-what-exactly-caused-the-longest-nationwide-ground-stop-in-25-years" /><summary type="html">After a nearly five-hour ground stoppage, flights in the US have resumed. However, officials are warning that it will take days to recover from the ongoing delays related to the incident. Transport Secretary Sean Duffy explained the crisis was due to a failure in ageing telecommunications equipment. What exactly happened? Answers with FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Shirli Sitbon.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Transport Secretary asks Congress for $30 billion to upgrade aviation infrastructure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8eabd1df91d18e6eb890c0f21048146375f0f26e6b740ea6f7a117f088515df</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T16:32:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-transport-secretary-asks-congress-for-30-bn-to-upgrade-aviation-infrastructure--1fa408877d9b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-transport-secretary-asks-congress-for-30-bn-to-upgrade-aviation-infrastructure" /><summary type="html">A failure in aging telecommunications equipment Friday forced a nationwide halt to departures from US airports. Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin says officials have found no evidence so far of a cyberattack, but that they're not ruling it out. Details by Jack Pownall.</summary></entry><entry><title>Copper wires blamed for US travel chaos as Trump asks Congress for money to overhaul system</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6082027bcb6dcd0089397e5ca22934f1219576716b63e512876193e3aba81e5</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T15:35:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261114-copper-wires-to-blame-for-us-flight-disruption-says-trump-administration--d2146e285ca6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261114-copper-wires-to-blame-for-us-flight-disruption-says-trump-administration" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration on Sunday pointed to aging infrastructure – specifically "a botched replacement of old copper wire communication lines" – as being responsible for the nationwide ground stop that snarled airline travel over the weekend. The president himself blamed the administration of his predecessor Joe Biden, in his first comments on the issue after a two-day silence.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>USA: All passengers survive after tanker hits docked river cruise ship in New Orleans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b29ef5e77a95b0c765a8569d8c9a56b380849e14385904ce6273b6182d115049</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T13:15:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/usa-all-passengers-survive-after-tanker-hits-docked-river-cruise-ship-in-new-orleans--196361a3fb34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/usa-all-passengers-survive-after-tanker-hits-docked-river-cruise-ship-in-new-orleans" /><summary type="html">A portion of the Mississippi River remains closed after a collision between an oil tanker and a riverboat forced a chaotic river rescue in Louisiana. Story by Caitlin Brown.</summary></entry><entry><title>Who are the 'street medics' showing up at protests around the world?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fbcedc71330d6d98a5fc56b67fbe933eceafa66a9c2cf6ef7026a23f5cf90a08</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T12:19:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/who-are-the-street-medics-showing-up-at-protests-around-the-world--0c414d784e65.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/who-are-the-street-medics-showing-up-at-protests-around-the-world" /><summary type="html">From treating tear gas exposure to tending to injuries, street medics have become an increasingly common sight at protests all over the world. But who exactly are they and when did they start showing up at demonstrations? Story by Daniel Quinlan.</summary></entry><entry><title>Half a million people gather for an open-air mass by Pope Leo in Peru</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3077714c2ee9815820527f38f9b9d2d22d02206df67a6fb552944f3d2d939163</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T11:17:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/half-a-million-people-gather-for-an-open-air-mass-by-pope-leo-in-peru--865ee0c1d4cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/half-a-million-people-gather-for-an-open-air-mass-by-pope-leo-in-peru" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo said it was a "joy to be back" in his second home of Chiclayo, where he made his name as a bishop. This is the latest stop on his South America tour, the very tour that saw fears of cancellation after the Pope underwent surgery for lung cancer. Story by Vedika Bahl.</summary></entry><entry><title>US nationwide flight ground stop: "Our routers got overloaded with data"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa47bd77ccbd1bc9fc58497fa52001933188f664c951e45b3bcfb767ed4e4377</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:14:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-nationwide-flight-ground-stop-our-routers-got-overloaded-with-data--86cafb111fce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-nationwide-flight-ground-stop-our-routers-got-overloaded-with-data" /><summary type="html">On Friday, the Federal Aviation Administration issued a rare nationwide ground stop. More than 8,200 flights, or over 31% of those scheduled in the United States, were canceled. The ground stop lasted nearly five hours and was the longest in the country since September 11, 2001. Officials blamed outdated air traffic communications equipment, and said that there was no evidence of a cyber attack. The airspace is now reopened and flights have resumed.</summary></entry><entry><title>US flights resume after nationwide ground stop lifted</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb9e6dea8386b7891675002cb512a840fef021f5167b0c91fa417363df98c9ed</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T02:35:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261114-us-flights-resume-after-nationwide-ground-stop-lifted-aviation--ee4c7a228fe5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261114-us-flights-resume-after-nationwide-ground-stop-lifted-aviation" /><summary type="html">The United States on Friday lifted an hours-long ground stop at the nation's airports, with top officials explaining that the disruption was not due to a cyberattack or a sweeping Microsoft outage. Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said that US airspace was now "opened up," and blamed "old hardware" for the travel chaos.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Passengers face further disruption as US flights slowly resume after ground stop</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d8b6d0d74001d622f8360bd89061d07ead149543bbe09a71cca8ab2a64f48377</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T22:43:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-us-air-travel-resumption-will-take-time-after-hours-long-stop--a75173ff3015.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-us-air-travel-resumption-will-take-time-after-hours-long-stop" /><summary type="html">While flights in the United States started resuming on Saturday following the longest nationwide ground stop in 25 years, more than 2,000 flights have been cancelled as airlines work to return to normal operations. Nearly 6,000 flights were cancelled on Friday, with the incident marking only the second time such an alert had been issued in US airspace since the 9/11 attacks.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US flight authority orders national ground stop over air traffic control 'communication issue'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a830f71f4aa8679f42b758968c34f6bcc55b2180ea14cdfb9eaa1f59023ab5e7</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T21:27:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-us-flight-authority-orders-national-ground-stop-over-air-traffic-control-communication-issu--bea6c8926b2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-us-flight-authority-orders-national-ground-stop-over-air-traffic-control-communication-issue" /><summary type="html">The US flight authority on Friday halted flights across the nation due to what US Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said was a communication issue affecting the country's air traffic control centres.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>The Nvidia affair: Are markets about to fall out of love with AI?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e40d2bbf08da1d67fe7e7a332d1179bdfd587b096a82d26cb85d8ee18c5a6b7</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T17:02:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-the-nvidia-affair-are-markets-about-to-fall-out-of-love-with-ai--afdd33fb8417.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-the-nvidia-affair-are-markets-about-to-fall-out-of-love-with-ai" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang’s departure from Nvidia exposes the vulnerabilities behind the AI boom. As equities reel in response to his resignation following extramarital affairs, alleged Chinese espionage and a summons to testify before US lawmakers, questions mount over who is really in charge of tech and whether the immense capital riding on it can survive the turmoil.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Haitian forces recapture national stadium after two years of gang control</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d3829a60ee85e967d8d1ad0c03b6e98db4006c46ac83f96aa380e8fb0ed4bc3d</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:09:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-haitian-forces-recapture-national-stadium-after-two-years-of-gang-control--cac3a4adff3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-haitian-forces-recapture-national-stadium-after-two-years-of-gang-control" /><summary type="html">Haitian security forces regained control Thursday, November 12, of the country's main stadium that had been under gang control for two years, forcing the national football team to play elsewhere. The Haitian National Police said in a statement that it had taken "full control" of the venue with the Task Force, a private security group serving the government, after which it left the stadium under the guard of Salvadoran soldiers.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Devastated wasteland': Haitian security forces regain control of stadium from gangs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2727b6766103baf1ee5322ecc338cec3fabfaed0f77805e728a7f6e69d57eb4a</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T14:37:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-devastated-wasteland-haitian-security-forces-regain-control-of-stadium-from-gangs--b069dccdf1c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-devastated-wasteland-haitian-security-forces-regain-control-of-stadium-from-gangs" /><summary type="html">Haitian security forces said they have regained control of the country's main stadium, wresting it back from the gangs that have been using it for the past two years. They were assisted by the Task Force, a private security group serving the government. The stadium is now under the guard of Salvadoran soldiers. FRANCE 24's senior reporter Catherine Norris Trent, who has covered Haiti extensively, said re-taking the stadium would be a significant step in an area of the city that had been a "devastated wasteland".</summary></entry><entry><title>Midterms: What does the 'blue tsunami' mean for US media?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92f2fda4eb9c7593afd927791c4475e998e98bfc6acc3090fd713f4e8c0bd19f</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T14:22:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261113-what-does-the-blue-tsunami-mean-for-us-media--9254bf757b1c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261113-what-does-the-blue-tsunami-mean-for-us-media" /><summary type="html">This week, FRANCE 24's media show Scoop looks at the impact of the midterm elections in the United States. While the results are being reckoned with by Republicans and celebrated by Democrats, what does it all mean for the press? Some media analysts wonder whether certain outlets, particularly ones accused of being cosy with the Trump administration, will change their tone. Our guest this week is International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert.</summary><category term="Scoop" /></entry></feed>
